course: dictionary
lesson: 13571
title: Inaugurate: starting something new
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To inaugurate something means to open or start it officially, often at a ceremony. Look at the clues around it: «The mayor will inaugurate the new library on Saturday.» A library is a building, and a mayor is an important person, so inaugurate must mean to open it officially.
explain: Inaugurate can also mean to swear a new leader into an important job. «The new president was inaugurated in a grand ceremony.» The job and the ceremony are the clues, so this meaning is about becoming a leader, not about a building.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. «The mayor will open the new library on Saturday» still makes sense, so open is a good match. Inaugurate is a more formal word, and you will meet it most in the news and in history lessons.
fact: Inaugurate is a verb: inaugurate, inaugurates, inaugurated, inaugurating.
fact: «Inaugurate» means to open or start something officially, often with a ceremony.
fact: «Inaugurate» can mean to swear a new leader into office, such as a US president.
fact: «Inaugurate» can also mean to begin a new period or system, as in «inaugurate a new era».
fact: In the US, presidents are inaugurated on 20 January after an election, and that day is called Inauguration Day.
exercise: «The mayor will inaugurate the new hospital on Friday.» What does inaugurate mean here? | To sell it to a school | To knock it down | To paint it red | *To open it officially
exercise: «The newly elected leader will be inaugurated in January.» What is happening to the leader? | Losing the election | *Being sworn into office at a formal ceremony | Writing a letter to the newspaper | Going on a long holiday
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to inaugurate when a new bridge is opened for the first time? | close | lose | *launch | hide
test: «The class will inaugurate a new reading corner today.» What does inaugurate mean? | *To start it officially | To repair it | To remove it | To hide it
test: «The team wanted to inaugurate a new era of teamwork.» What does inaugurate mean here? | To end the game | To count the points | To forget the rules | *To begin a new period
exam: In «The president was inaugurated on Monday», what has happened? | A president went to sleep | *A new leader was sworn into office | A president lost a game | A president went shopping
